BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mythology and folklore reading group: Power
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T201500
UID:6ac692389d27a000454f4f17@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Our November session will include stories on the theme of Powe
 r from around the world.\nToronto Reference Library invites you to join th
 e Mythology and Folktale reading group. The group will meet once a month t
 o read aloud and discuss famous and lesser known myths. No pre-reading req
 uired\, beginners welcome.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal i
 nformation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under t
 he Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informat
 ion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and ev
 aluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be 
 directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 
 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Founder's room\, first floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac692389d27a000454f4f17
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Silver Screamers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T200000
UID:6aba9faac6cddb004594ea3a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Silver Screamers is a heartwarming and spine-tingling new docu
 mentary that follows a spirited group of older adults who set out to make 
 a horror film\, stepping far outside their comfort zones.\nLed by a local 
 filmmaker\, they navigate the challenges of low-budget movie-making with h
 umour\, heart\, and resilience.  Along the way\, they discover newfound co
 nfidence\, forge meaningful friendships\, and prove that creativity knows 
 no age.\nThe filmmaker\, Sean Cisterna\, will lead a discussion and Q&A ab
 out the film and its topics and themes.
LOCATION:New Toronto
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aba9faac6cddb004594ea3a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Polish Book Club Discussion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T153000
UID:696ba4606724c63d00ecaf8b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Polish Reading Club. Have your recently read a book that you w
 ant others to know about. This is a  meeting and place for a conversati
 on with those who read in Polish. It doesn't matter what you read\;  book
 s or magazines\, fiction or popular science. Come and tell us what you are
  reading and why.\nIt's a wonderful opportunity to hear about reading pass
 ions and a place to meet new friends.\nKlub czytajacych po polsku. Spotkan
 ie i rozmowa z tymi co czytaja po polsku.
LOCATION:Long Branch\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696ba4606724c63d00ecaf8b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
