BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners: Use the Internet
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T150000
UID:6aadbc0c19094f0c6938e342@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An introductory class on the Internet for absolute beginners w
 ith little computer experience.\nIn this session you will:\nUnderstand how
  to read a web site address\nPractice using web addresses\nSearch for info
 rmation using a search engine\nExplore a web site in detail to understand 
 its key components\nUpon completion of this class students will be able to
  use the internet at a beginner level and complete simple searches.\nPrere
 quisites: Computer for Beginners - Use the Mouse & Keyboard or basic mous
 e and keyboarding skills\nFormat: Hands-on with demonstrations.\nDrop-in p
 rogram. Space is limited.
LOCATION:Jane/Sheppard
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aadbc0c19094f0c6938e342
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adult Crafternoon Social
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T153000
UID:6ac94070ebad2200454442ac@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us every month at the College/Shaw Library for our Adult
  Crafternoon Social!\nDrop in for some coffee and light music while explor
 ing your creative abilities with a simple craft or art project. A great op
 portunity to socialize in a relaxed and friendly space. Materials provided
 \, but feel free to bring in something you're already working on!\nWed Nov
  25 - Christmas Crafts\nWed Dec 30 - Collage
LOCATION:College/Shaw\, Basement auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac94070ebad2200454442ac
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Our Urban Forest
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T123000
UID:6a8e1c354995480655ec7358@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Toronto has one of the largest urban forests in the world. Joi
 n the\nCity of Toronto Urban Forestry\nteam\nfor an in-library presentatio
 n on this amazing natural habitat that reaches all corners of Toronto.\nWe
 ’ll talk about what makes the urban forest so special and share tools to
  explore and understand it better. Bring questions and curiosities and lea
 ve with emboldened confidence and understanding of your City and the natur
 al world that surrounds you!\nNo registration required\; Drop-in until roo
 m is at full capacity\nThis program is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\n
 program series\, supported by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Ch
 apter.​
LOCATION:Flemingdon Park\, Library Auditorium (2nd Floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8e1c354995480655ec7358
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
