BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Orchid: Daunting Diva\, Evocative Evolutionary or Humble House
 plant?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T193000
UID:6abe8b7f377296003a48eb53@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Orchid is now the world's MOST popular houseplant. Facilit
 ated by a Toronto Master Gardener\, learn fascinating stories\, fun facts 
 and tips on orchid care. Love them already but yours don't bloom? Don't fr
 et! We have answers. Have disease and pest problems? We help you solve th
 em. Plus\, the best orchids to grow in your home. Suitable for gardeners o
 f any skill level.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informati
 on on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Publi
 c Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will
  only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation
 . Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed
  to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge St
 reet\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albion\, Program Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abe8b7f377296003a48eb53
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
