BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:COSTI: Program for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T150000
UID:6ac95b65035faf0033db8ca1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for presentations\non what is needed to compile your 
 Will and Power of Attorney\, this\nevent is designed to support seniors in
  our community.\nViviana Filazzola\, COSTI Elderly Persons’ Centre Co-or
 dinator\, will share information on community programs and benefits availa
 ble to seniors. You will learn about tips for maintaining wellness and so
 cial connection\, information on pensions\, health services\, local suppor
 ts and how to access resources in your community.\nDrop In Program. No Reg
 istration Required.
LOCATION:Humber Summit\, Auditorium\, Lower Level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac95b65035faf0033db8ca1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seniors E-Connect
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T170000
UID:6a84859f69166f088b930bba@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you 55+? Do you have a phone\, tablet or computer you don'
 t know how to use or want to learn to use better? Do you enjoy meeting new
  people?\nSeniors E-Connect will help you learn tech topics in a fun group
  setting\, but with the one-on-one help of a teen volunteer under the gui
 dance of library staff. Learn the basics of using computers\, tablets and 
 smartphones and popular websites and software.\nIf you're a teen between t
 he ages of 13-17 and would like to learn more about becoming a Seniors E-C
 onnect volunteer\, visit the\nSeniors E-Connect Volunteering page\nor cont
 act the branch.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Bagshaw Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a84859f69166f088b930bba
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
