BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AI Robot mBot2: Sightseeing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T151500
UID:6a92f93d2dac6e00372295b4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Take your mBot2 on a robotic sightseeing adventure! Learn how 
 to program the robot to follow a path\, recognize different colors\, and p
 erform special actions along the way. A fun challenge that brings coding a
 nd robotics together.\nDetails:  patrons aged 18+\, basic mouse and keybo
 arding skills required\, some experience with block coding is beneficial
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Multi-Purpose Room\, 1st Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a92f93d2dac6e00372295b4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Death Café
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T200000
UID:6a909d1e3b6c71003e5bd9ea@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A Death Café is a gathering of people\, often strangers\, who
  will drink tea\, have a snack and discuss death together. The aim is to i
 ncrease the awareness of death with a view to helping people make the most
  of their lives. Discussions will be in small groups with no agenda\, no o
 bjectives and no particular theme. Prepare to hear and tell stories.\nThis
  is not a grief support or counselling session. The facilitators for this 
 Death Café are Nadine Lavoie and Andrea Skitch.\nDrop-in\, but space is l
 imited.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a909d1e3b6c71003e5bd9ea
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
