BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Housing Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261223T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261223T170000
UID:6abc17ba377296003a48773a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drop in and work one-on-one with staff from The Housing Help C
 entre (THHC) to determine your housing needs\, connect you to other govern
 ment services\, and to match you with landlords across the city. THHC work
 s with both individuals and families in the City of Toronto to find and ma
 intain affordable\, safe housing.\nThe Housing Help Centre can be contacte
 d at 416-285-8070 or at shhc.ca.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Front Entrance
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc17ba377296003a48773a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Retirement Planning
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T200000
UID:6a8ca2332656cb00467289c7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:November is Financial Literacy Month.\nPresented by Riverdal
 e Immigrant Women's Centre\, this workshop is an introduction to long-term
  financial planning including retirement savings and better understanding 
 of federal income benefits\, such as\, Canada Pension Plan (CPP) and Old A
 ge Security (OAS). Drop-in program\, first come\, first serve seating.
LOCATION:Mount Dennis\, Lower Level\, Room 2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8ca2332656cb00467289c7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
