BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:*FULL -Human Connection 101 Workshop Series for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T150000
UID:6ac407bf686221156abb5676@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Human connection has a profound impact on our health and happi
 ness\, especially in our increasingly disconnected world. Join GenWell in 
 an interactive 5-week (Oct 1\, 8\, 15\, 22 & 29) program series to learn p
 ractical ways to enhance social health\, understand the adverse effects of
  loneliness\, and discover the benefits of building more meaningful connec
 tions. Receive a free social health workbook\, spend time with other parti
 cipants after the workshops\, and enjoy some light refreshments provided.\
 nAbout GenWell: Founded in 2016\, GenWell is a registered charity whose mi
 ssion is to make the world a happier and healthier place by educating\, em
 powering\, and catalyzing forty million Canadians about the importance of 
 their social health.\nRegistration full.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac407bf686221156abb5676
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Housing Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T170000
UID:6abc17ba377296003a487734@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drop in and work one-on-one with staff from The Housing Help C
 entre (THHC) to determine your housing needs\, connect you to other govern
 ment services\, and to match you with landlords across the city. THHC work
 s with both individuals and families in the City of Toronto to find and ma
 intain affordable\, safe housing.\nThe Housing Help Centre can be contacte
 d at 416-285-8070 or at shhc.ca.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Front Entrance
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc17ba377296003a487734
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adult Crafternoon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T153000
UID:6a7b75fa4c610f0038947889@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Craft and socialize in a friendly and welcoming environment at
  our monthly adult and seniors crafternoon!\nConsider wearing clothes that
  you don't mind getting messy.\nOctober\n- Cork Pumpkin\nNovember\n- Holid
 ay Ornament\nDecember - Step-By-Step Acrylic Painting – Holiday Edition
 \nJoin us for a self-guided painting program. Create wintery artwork at y
 our own pace using printed instructions provided by library staff. All mat
 erials are supplied in this encouraging\, social\, and flexible environmen
 t of creative exploration.\nDrop in. Space is limited to 25 participants. 
  Arrive early to secure a spot!
LOCATION:Richview\, Room A\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7b75fa4c610f0038947889
