BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Library Social Spot : Bone Health 101
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T150000
UID:6aac0ab26059b704112ae741@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:At least 1 in 3 women and 1 in 5 men will suffer from a fragil
 ity fracture in their lifetime. Join a volunteer facilitator from Osteopor
 osis Canada and learn how to improve your bone health\, reduce your risk o
 f osteoporosis and related fractures.\nThis is a Drop In program.
LOCATION:Ethennonnhawahstihnen'
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aac0ab26059b704112ae741
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Writers Collective of Canada (WCC): Community Writing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T200000
UID:6abfc99029c3d600332d2c37@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Experience the transformative power of writing in an inclusive
  space!\nA\nWriters Collective of Canada (WCC)\nworkshop is unlike any oth
 er. We write together\, share first drafts in an encouraging environment\,
  listen deeply to one another\, and receive supportive feedback. Tap into 
 your story and explore your voice in an environment of dignity\, courage\,
  and respect.\nNo experience required. Beginners are welcome. Materials ar
 e provided. Workshops are not sequential\; every workshop is unique - join
  in at any session and let's write together!\nDrop in\, no registration re
 quired\n. Please arrive a few minutes early. For more information\, please
  contact the branch.\n​Presented by Writers Collective of Canada (WCC)\,
  a charitable arts-health organization that ignites connection through cre
 ativity by inspiring powerful\, authentic stories shared in community.\nht
 tps://wcc-cec.org/
LOCATION:Evelyn Gregory
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abfc99029c3d600332d2c37
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tea and Entertainment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T160000
UID:6a774d824523092f0035ae9e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy watching DVDs in the Library Auditorium.\nCoffee\, tea a
 nd cookies or snacks will be served after the film.  Ingredient lists will
  be available upon request.\\\nBeyond the Now\nWhat if the future isn't so
 mething that happens to us—but something we can shape? Explore bold idea
 s\, inspiring innovators and practical solutions that challenge us to thin
 k beyond today and imagine a better tomorrow. Closed Captions. 53 minutes.
  2024.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a774d824523092f0035ae9e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tea & Entertainment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261113T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261113T160000
UID:6a774c9af4e5db3d00c75042@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy watching DVDs in the Library Auditorium.\nCoffee\, tea a
 nd cookies or snacks will be served after the film.  Ingredient lists will
  be available upon request.\nThe Last Surviving Cheetahs\nThis film follow
 s the search for the critically endangered Asiatic cheetah in the remote d
 eserts of Iran. This powerful documentary captures the struggle to protect
  one of the world’s rarest big cats before it disappears forever. 55 min
 utes. 2025
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a774c9af4e5db3d00c75042
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tea and Entertainment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T160000
UID:6a774ad19006f7535315d44b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy watching DVDs in the Library Auditorium.\nCoffee\, tea a
 nd cookies or snacks will be served after the film.  Ingredient lists will
  be available upon request\nLook Who’s Driving\nCompanies are developing
  self driving cars and many are already on the road.\nAre they safer than 
 those driven by humans? Explore the future of this technology. Closed capt
 ions.53 minutes. 2019
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a774ad19006f7535315d44b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
