DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T200000
UID:6a9b1b7c36204e08fbb9a58c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Editor Gregory Klages presents\nAlgonquin Diaries\n(Dinerva\, 
 2025)\, compiling the diary entries of Mark Robinson about life in Algonqu
 in Park in the early 20th century. Over three decades\, Robinson served as
  a Ranger\, Acting Park Superintendent\, and officer in the Canadian Exped
 itionary Force. Throughout\, he maintained daily diaries in which he recor
 ded his experiences of significant social\, political\, cultural\, and env
 ironmental events.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informati
 on on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Publi
 c Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will
  only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation
 . Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed
