BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toronto's Ravines
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T170000
UID:6ab565f6ca248a0029182aae@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Toronto's ravine landscapes are not just a sanctuary for wildl
 ife\; they also protect the city against flooding and allow us to enjoy na
 ture at our doorsteps. This presentation by the Toronto Field Naturalists 
 shares how the ravines are changing over time\; how they are responding to
  numerous pressures and how you can explore and help protect them.\nPresen
 ter Bio:\nEllen Schwartzel is a former president of the Toronto Field Natu
 ralists\, and she enjoys leading walks through Toronto's ravines.  Ellen's
  career in environmental policy included 23 years with the Environmental C
 ommissioner of Ontario. She was Ontario's Deputy Environmental Commissione
 r for four years\, until retiring in 2018.  Ellen’s academic training wa
 s in Botany\, and she received her BSc and MSc at the University of Toront
 o.\nDrop In\, No Registration is Required.\nPlease contact Long Branch\, 4
 16-394-5320 with any inquiries.
LOCATION:Long Branch
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab565f6ca248a0029182aae
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:4th Monday Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261214T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261214T153000
UID:6a3056badcc1022f0039ae27@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to\nDeer Park's 4th Monday Book Club\n! We meet monthl
 y to discuss a variety of books chosen by our members.\n2026 Schedule:\nJa
 n. 26.\nQuiet\nby Susan Cain\nFeb. 23.\nThe Rosie Project\nby Graeme Simsi
 on\nMar. 23.\nThe Marriage of Opposites\nby Alice Hoffman\nApr. 27.\nThe B
 ook of Eels\nby Patrik Svensson\nMay 25.\nTrust\nby Hernan Diaz\nJun. 22.\
 nReproduction\nby Ian Williams\nJul. 27.\nCrow Lake\nby Mary Lawson\nAug. 
 24.\nUntil August\nby Gabriel Garcia Marquez\nSep. 28.\nNever Let Me Go\nb
 y Kazuo Ishiguro\nOct. 26.\nBook Selection for Monday Book Club 2027\nThis
  meeting will take place in the Main Floor Program Room\nNov. 23.\nBehind 
 the Beautiful Forevers\nby Katherine Boo\n*Dec. 14.\nMaybe You Should Talk
  to Someone\nby Lori Gottlieb\n*October 26th is a change in the usual Prog
 ram Room since Deer Park is acting as a voting poll that day\n*December 14
 th is a change from the usual schedule\, to accommodate the holiday season
 \nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is
  collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, 
 sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for 
 event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about 
 how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline sta
 ff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON 
 M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Deer Park\, Room 204\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3056badcc1022f0039ae27
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
