BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP) for Healthy Aging
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261115T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261115T163000
UID:6ac902fa295b3b0033cb0d59@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for anyone looking to strengthen their well-being
 —whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or s
 imply wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. The WRA
 P for Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP) Workshop for Healthy Aging is e
 xpertly designed by Hope + Me for individuals aged 60 and older using the 
 principles of WRAP\, but with scenarios and tools focused on common aging 
 challenges.\nThis 3-week session is appropriate for people with no experie
 nce with WRAP\, or for those who wish to refresh their knowledge and skill
 s.\nParticipants will receive a certificate of participation upon program 
 completion\, but these sessions do not contribute to a WRAP certificate. F
 ind more WRAP program options at TPL\nhere.\nThis WRAP Group meets every S
 unday\, once a week for 3 weeks November 8 - November 22. Week 1 will be 
 3 hours\, with a 30 minute overview and orientation of  WRAP\; Weeks 2 and
  3 will be 2.5 hours.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provided\n.\nSnacks and 
 refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be
  available at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nHope 
 + Me\n. Hope + Me is solely responsible for the protection of personal inf
 ormation collected through the program registration process.
LOCATION:Locke\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac902fa295b3b0033cb0d59
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Golden Paintbrush: Painting Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T143000
UID:6abffb4f9abb62002c6bcc94@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A beginner-friendly acrylic painting class where no experience
  is necessary—just a willingness to have fun and try something new. Each
  session\, you'll be guided step-by-step through a simple project by a sup
 portive instructor. Learn the basics of color mixing\, brush techniques\, 
 and composition\, while creating your own beautiful artwork to take home. 
 All materials—including paints\, brushes\, canvases\, and aprons—will 
 be provided by the presenter. Just bring your creativity and a smile!
LOCATION:Spadina Road\, Centre of branch at Canoe table
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abffb4f9abb62002c6bcc94
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tea and Entertainment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261204T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261204T160000
UID:6a774fccf4e5db3d00c7507b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy watching DVDs in the Library Auditorium.\nCoffee\, tea a
 nd cookies or snacks will be served after the film.\nIngredient lists will
  be available upon request.\nExtremes\nVenture out on  a breathtaking jou
 rney into Earth’s most extreme environments\, from vast underground cave
 s and frozen Arctic tundra to scorching deserts and remote mountain peaks.
  Discover the remarkable animals that survive against incredible odds\, sh
 owcasing nature’s resilience\, adaptation and the growing challenges pos
 ed by a changing climate. Closed captions. 58 minutes.2025
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a774fccf4e5db3d00c7507b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Grown-ups Reading Children's Literature Book Club: Mary Norton's B
 orrowers (Book 1)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T160000
UID:6a7bb64daafa6100295c051b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the monthly meeting of Osborne Collection Grown-up
 s Reading Children's Literature Book Club. It is for adult readers who enj
 oy children's books. Revisit favourite stories of your childhood or read m
 ore or less known notable books for young readers for the first time.\nThe
  Borrowers\nNovember 14: Borrowers Book 1 by Mary Norton\nDecember 5: The
  BFG by Roald Dahl\nJanuary 9 (2027): Number the Stars by Lois Lowry
