BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AI for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T160000
UID:6a9c32d660ccaf01c0238f1c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Staying connected with family\, keeping track of appointments\
 , finding programs that interest you. AI can help with everyday things. No
  jargon\, no pressure\, no experience needed.\nIn this class led by our In
 novator-in-Residence\,\nRyan Kelln\n\, you'll learn how AI can help you w
 rite a message in your own voice\, turn a spoken thought into a checklist\
 , plan questions for an appointment\, and find community programs. We'll a
 lso talk straight about the risks: AI that sounds like a person deserves c
 aution\, and we'll practice spotting the scams that use it. You'll leave w
 ith large-print materials\, one personally useful template\, and a simple 
 family safety phrase\, all at your own pace.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyb
 oarding and internet skills. Computers are provided. No coding experienc
 e required.\nRegistration is required and will start September 9\, 2026 at
  9:00 AM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the s
 tart of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seats will be filled on 
 a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is reached. If you wish t
 o save your work from this hands-on program\, please bring your own USB st
 ick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program includes activ
 ities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou do
  not need to create your own account for this program.\nParticipants are e
 ncouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\, which 
 include best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review the privac
 y statements of each tool prior to attending this program:\nClaude Code\nL
 earn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nClaude Cowork\nLearn more
  about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle Antigravity\nLearn more abo
 ut the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more about the
  tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal
  information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under
  the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inform
 ation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and 
 evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can b
 e directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 78
 9 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9c32d660ccaf01c0238f1c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
