DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261031T113000
UID:6ab1acd03dd190003e739cde@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Did you know that nearly one third of Canadian Small Businesse
 s fail within the first 5 years?\n[1]\nThis conversation circle invites me
 mbers of the public to share and reflect on their experiences of professio
 nal and business failure in a non-judgemental environment.\nNo happy endin
 gs are required!\nCoffee\, tea and snacks are provided.\nRegistration is e
 ncouraged.\nDrop-ins welcome until capacity is reached. Attendees can shar
 e their stories with the group\, or just come to listen.\n[1]\nKey Small B
 usiness Statistics 2024\n. 1 Apr. 2025\,\nhttps://ised-isde.canada.ca/site
 /sme-research-statistics/en/key-small-business-statistics/key-small-busine
 ss-statistics-2024\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal inform
 ation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Pu
 blic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information w
 ill only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluat
 ion. Questions about how the library handles your information can be direc
 ted to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge
  Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 2/3 \n(on the 2nd floor on the 
 west side side of the Library)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab1acd03dd190003e739cde
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
