BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:*FULL -Human Connection 101 Workshop Series for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T150000
UID:6ac407bf686221156abb5675@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Human connection has a profound impact on our health and happi
 ness\, especially in our increasingly disconnected world. Join GenWell in 
 an interactive 5-week (Oct 1\, 8\, 15\, 22 & 29) program series to learn p
 ractical ways to enhance social health\, understand the adverse effects of
  loneliness\, and discover the benefits of building more meaningful connec
 tions. Receive a free social health workbook\, spend time with other parti
 cipants after the workshops\, and enjoy some light refreshments provided.\
 nAbout GenWell: Founded in 2016\, GenWell is a registered charity whose mi
 ssion is to make the world a happier and healthier place by educating\, em
 powering\, and catalyzing forty million Canadians about the importance of 
 their social health.\nRegistration full.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac407bf686221156abb5675
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Writers Collective of Canada (WCC): Community Writing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T200000
UID:6abfc99029c3d600332d2c3b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Experience the transformative power of writing in an inclusive
  space!\nA\nWriters Collective of Canada (WCC)\nworkshop is unlike any oth
 er. We write together\, share first drafts in an encouraging environment\,
  listen deeply to one another\, and receive supportive feedback. Tap into 
 your story and explore your voice in an environment of dignity\, courage\,
  and respect.\nNo experience required. Beginners are welcome. Materials ar
 e provided. Workshops are not sequential\; every workshop is unique - join
  in at any session and let's write together!\nDrop in\, no registration re
 quired\n. Please arrive a few minutes early. For more information\, please
  contact the branch.\n​Presented by Writers Collective of Canada (WCC)\,
  a charitable arts-health organization that ignites connection through cre
 ativity by inspiring powerful\, authentic stories shared in community.\nht
 tps://wcc-cec.org/
LOCATION:Evelyn Gregory
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abfc99029c3d600332d2c3b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
