BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Map It": Community Mapping & Data Storytelling
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T200000
UID:6a9c73f336204e08fbb9db02@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Your neighbourhood tells a story and the data to prove it alre
 ady exists. In this three-session series\, you will learn to find real civ
 ic data about your community\, plot it on an interactive map\, and turn wh
 at you discover into a powerful advocacy piece. No technical experience ne
 eded. Just curiosity about where you live and a desire to make it better.\
 nArrive 30 minutes before or stay 30 minutes after the program for one-on-
 one consultations.\nThis program is part of TPL's Innovator in Residence s
 eries focused on civic innovation. From October 5 to November 28\, join pr
 ograms\, workshops and one-on-one consultations led by technology strategi
 st Ismail Mohamud to learn how technology can help you create positive cha
 nge in your community. Learn more at\ntpl.ca/iir\n.\nInformation Collectio
 n Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toron
 to Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\
 , and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regis
 tration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles
  your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.c
 a\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9c73f336204e08fbb9db02
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What is Artificial Intelligence?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T143000
UID:6ac91833ebad22004544365a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:AI technologies have become increasingly prevalent in many asp
 ects of modern life\, including healthcare\, finance\, transportation\, an
 d entertainment. Some examples of AI applications include virtual assistan
 ts like Siri and Alexa\, self-driving cars\, fraud detection systems\, and
  personalized recommendations in online shopping. Come join this beginner 
 in-person class to learn what AI is\, how it learns and predicts outcomes\
 , considerations when using GenAI applications\, and how the Internet of T
 hings (IOT) applies to AI.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal i
 nformation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under t
 he Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informat
 ion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and ev
 aluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be 
 directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 
 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Woodside Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac91833ebad22004544365a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
