BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What is Artificial Intelligence?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T153000
UID:6ab6e6cb101eb7003f32f4c9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:AI technologies have become increasingly prevalent in many asp
 ects of modern life\, including healthcare\, finance\, transportation\, an
 d entertainment. Some examples of AI applications include virtual assistan
 ts like Siri and Alexa\, self-driving cars\, fraud detection systems\, and
  personalized recommendations in online shopping. Come join this beginner 
 in-person class to learn what AI is\, how it learns and predicts outcomes\
 , considerations when using GenAI applications\, and how the Internet of T
 hings (IOT) applies to AI.\nRegistration is required.\nInformation Collect
 ion Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Tor
 onto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c
 )\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program reg
 istration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handl
 es your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl
 .ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Learning Center 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6e6cb101eb7003f32f4c9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Health Support Table with SCHC
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T150000
UID:6a908e4236204e08fbb7a693@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come and have a conversation with health team from the Scarbor
 ough Centre for Healthy Communities (SCHC) to learn and get connected to a
  variety of health care services.\nGet support with navigating services li
 ke:\n- Cancer Screening information and referrals\n- Diabetes Education\n-
  Preventative Care\n- Vaccination Awareness\n- Mental Health\n- Connection
 s to Community Support services\nDrop-in\, no registration required. Regul
 ar visits second Wednesday of each month in the library foyer.
