BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Privacy 101
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T153000
UID:6aad84b0f9ed2e003851bad9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested to learn how to maintain your online privac
 y and how to secure your online accounts and devices? If so\, this is the 
 class for you. Come and join us in this introductory session that is fille
 d with hands-on activities and discussion.\nIn this program\, you will:\nL
 earn how to maintain your online privacy through good habits and the secur
 ity of your accounts and devices.\nDevelop a strong password\, and review 
 the best methods for storing your passwords.\nLearn about various online t
 hreats: malware\, phishing\, hacking\, etc.\nGain an understanding of the 
 limitations of these tools and habits.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nTh
 e personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Lib
 rary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). 
 The information will only be used for event and program registration\, del
 ivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informa
 tion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397
 -5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aad84b0f9ed2e003851bad9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google Docs 1: Create and Edit a File
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T153000
UID:6aab2d608cf597003f946864@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how Google Docs can be a useful free tool when you don't
  have access to Microsoft Word. In this introductory class you will learn 
 how to open\, create\, save and delete Google Docs. Features such as highl
 ight\, bold\, italics\, underline\, font colour and font size will be cove
 red as well as how to use spell check\, print\, and download as Word docum
 ent.\nPrerequisites: Basic mouse and keyboard skills are required.\nFormat
 : Hands-on with demonstrations\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe person
 al information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library und
 er the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The info
 rmation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery an
 d evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can
  be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 
 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aab2d608cf597003f946864
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tuesday Night Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T194500
UID:6ab17d27ab7a8e0037c36757@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Please join us on Tuesday\, October 27\, to discuss our book o
 f the month\,\nBrother\n\,\nby David Chariandy\, winner of the\n2017 Roger
 s Writers' Trust Fiction Prize. This\nintensely beautiful\, powerful nov
 el explores questions of masculinity\, family\, race\, and identity as the
 y are played out in a Scarborough housing complex during the sweltering he
 at and simmering violence of the summer of 1991.\nGet a copy at the first-
 floor circulation desk at Maria A. Shchuka Library while supplies last\, 
 or place a hold on the book with your library card. Ask staff how to acce
 ss eBooks and eAudiobooks.\nDrop-in\, registration not required.\nFor more
  information\, please contact Maria A. Shchuka Library at 416-394-1000.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, First floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab17d27ab7a8e0037c36757
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T113000
UID:6aad3aa886d8450031170522@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Computers for Beginners 1: Use the Mouse\nA class on how to us
 e a mouse for absolute beginners with little or no computer experience.\nI
 n this first session you will:\nObserve and practice how to operate a mous
 e effectively\nUnderstand various mouse pointers and cursors\nReview basic
  keyboard functions\nUse the mouse for basic Windows functions\nUpon compl
 etion of this class students will be able to use a computer mouse at a bas
 ic level and will be able to go online for additional practice.\nComputers
  for Beginners 2: Use the Keyboard\nA class on basic keyboard functions fo
 r absolute beginners with little or no computer experience.\nIn this secon
 d session you will:\nFamiliarize yourself through practice with the most e
 ssential keyboard functions (alphabet\, number and symbol keys)\nPractice 
 proper keyboarding posture\nUpon completion of this class students will be
  able to use a keyboard at a beginner level and know how to go online for 
 additional practice.\nComputers for Beginners 3: Use the Internet\nAn intr
 oductory class on the Internet for absolute beginners with little computer
  experience.\nIn this fourth session you will:\nUnderstand how to read a w
 eb site address\nPractice using web addresses\nSearch for information usin
 g a search engine\nExplore a web site in detail to understand its key comp
 onents\nUpon completion of this class students will be able to use the int
 ernet at a beginner level and complete simple searches.\nComputers for Beg
 inners 4: Use Google Search and Maps\nA class on using Google's filters\, 
 tools\, and Maps for absolute beginners with little computer experience.\n
 In this fifth session you will:\nUse Google search tools more effectively 
 to find websites\, images\, and news sites\nExplore Google Maps to find ad
 dresses and get directions for transit and road travel.\nUpon completion o
 f this class students will be able to use more advanced search engine feat
 ures and use Google Maps at a basic level.\nComputers for Beginners 5: Use
  Windows\nA class on essential basic Windows skills for absolute beginners
  with little computer experience.\nIn this third session you will:\nBecome
  familiar with the Windows (10) operating system\nPractice using common Wi
 ndows features: File Explorer\, Desktop\, Taskbar\, Windows\, Applications
 \nUpon completion of this class students will have a basic understanding o
 f how to create and organize files in the Windows environment.
LOCATION:McGregor Park
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aad3aa886d8450031170522
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
