BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Word Basics 2: Format a Flyer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T153000
UID:6ab2b6b4ca248a002917983d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Build on your basic Microsoft Word skills and learn to use Wor
 d more effectively.\nIn this class\, you will:\nPractice new Word skills w
 hile you design a flyer\nFormat text\, margins\, indents\, headers and foo
 ters\nFormat text as columns\nCreate bulleted\, numbered and sorted lists\
 nReview your document with Spelling and Grammar check and Thesaurus\nUpon 
 completion of this class\, you will be able to use even more Word tools to
  design your documents.\nPrerequisites:  Word Basics 1 or equivalent skill
 s. Basic keyboarding and mouse skills required.\nFormat: Hands-on with dem
 onstrations\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Learning Centre 2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab2b6b4ca248a002917983d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
